--- note
### `compute_batch_loss` (75–88) & `_evaluate_pair` (91–109)
`compute_batch_loss` just slices each padded item back to its real `(n_t, n_t1)` size and averages
`compute_loss` over the batch. `_evaluate_pair` reuses `compute_loss` and adds an accuracy count
(`probs > 0.5` vs target) over the supervised mask — used only for reporting, never for backprop.
```python
def compute_batch_loss(logits, target, mask_t, mask_t1):
    B = logits.shape[0]; losses = []                          # one loss per batch item
    for b in range(B):
        nt  = mask_t[b].sum().item()                          # real node count, frame t
        nt1 = mask_t1[b].sum().item()                         # real node count, frame t+1
        losses.append(compute_loss(logits[b, :nt, :nt1], target[b, :nt, :nt1]))  # unpad + loss
    return torch.stack(losses).mean()                         # batch-mean link loss
```
